  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1255 PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nWeak ridging builds in midweek along with light westerly surface \nflow. This will help boost temperatures back into the 70s while also \nkeeping us dry. Flow aloft then transitions to the northwest later \nin the week allowing for a couple of weak cold fronts to move across \nthe region. Don't look for much change as core of colder air with \nthese stays well to our east. \n\nOur next storm system will arrive on the West Coast early next \nweekend before heading this direction. This system is expected to \nweaken before reaching us while maintaining warm conditions. Rain\nchances increasing slightly (20%) as the system moves through \nSunday, but for now, it looks like amounts will stay light.",
